course: dictionary
lesson: 11115
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Whistle can be a thing you blow, a high sound, or the act of making a tune. «The referee blew her whistle to start the game» shows you the object.
explain: «The kettle began to whistle as the water boiled.» Here whistle is the high sound, not a thing you hold. Look at the clues around it: a kettle and boiling water both point to a sound. Ask yourself which meaning would fit best.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «The kettle began to whistle» means the high sound, does it still make sense? Yes, so you have probably got it. If it does not fit, read on and look for more clues.
fact: A whistle is a small object you blow to make a loud, high sound.
fact: To whistle means to make a tune or a high sound by blowing air through your lips or a whistle.
fact: In sport, a referee blows a whistle to start and stop games.
fact: «Blow the whistle» is a phrase that means tell people about something wrong.
fact: Some animals whistle too: «Alpine marmots» whistle to warn each other of eagles and foxes.
exercise: «The referee blew her whistle to start the game.» What is a whistle here? | A tune you hum in the car | A kind of bird | A large wave in the sea | *A small object you blow to make a loud, high sound
exercise: «Dogs can hear a dog whistle that is too high for people to hear.» What does this tell you? | Dogs cannot hear anything at all | *Some sounds are too high for people to hear | Dogs cannot hear people | Whistles are always very quiet
exercise: Dad says, «Let's blow the whistle on that bully.» What does blow the whistle mean? | Play a tune on a flute | Shout for help from the top of a hill | Stop running and sit down | *Tell people about something wrong
test: «Alpine marmots whistle to warn each other of eagles and foxes.» Why do they whistle? | To tell a joke | *To warn each other of danger | To call for a swim | To sleep for six months
test: Kai says whistle is only ever a thing you blow. Is he right? | *No, whistle can also mean a high sound or making a tune | Yes, but only in football | Yes, it is only ever a thing | No, whistle means to fall asleep
exam: «After the final whistle your muscles need repairing, so a sandwich, pasta or a glass of milk helps.» What does the final whistle mean? | A bird's song in the morning | A small bottle of water | *The whistle that ends a game | A tune played after dinner
